.TH PREDATORPREY 1
.SH NAME
predatorprey \- Lotka-Volterra, plotted against its own rate
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B temple/predatorprey
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I PredatorPrey
is a port of the TempleOS
.B Demo/Graphics/PredatorPrey.HC
demonstration.
It runs under
.IR wm (1).
.PP
"Classic 2nd order nonlinear ordinary differential equation", integrated
by plain Euler at a millionth of a time unit with ten thousand of those
between plotted points.  What is plotted is not the populations against
time but each population against its own rate of change, which turns the
cycle into a closed loop; trajectory after trajectory starts from a
random pair and is drawn over the last, so the whole family of orbits
becomes visible.
.PP
The original runs one trajectory per core and waits on a bitmask.  Dis
execution here is serialised, so they run one after another, which
changes the order they appear in and nothing else.
.PP
The controls are:
.TF "any key"
.TP
.B "any key"
Dismiss the opening panel; another exits
.PD
.SH SOURCE
.B /appl/temple/predatorprey.b
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR temple (1),
.IR wm (1)
